From f7407fa03d55588618de529f28fb02a8f72ccb89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:57:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] asahi: hide VM status from virtio guests

The Vulkan driver checks the VM status after each wait with a
GET_PARAMS ioctl straight on the device fd. In a virtio guest that fd
is virtio-gpu, which has no such ioctl, so the very first fence wait
reported VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST.

Like the queue-limits query, these groups cannot be forwarded: drop
VM_STATUS and VM_STATUS_MIRROR from the features of virtio guests, so
the driver does not rely on them.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
---
 src/asahi/lib/agx_device.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/asahi/lib/agx_device.c b/src/asahi/lib/agx_device.c
index 0511b1c1..64f3287a 100644
--- a/src/asahi/lib/agx_device.c
+++ b/src/asahi/lib/agx_device.c
@@ -940,6 +940,13 @@ agx_open_device(void *memctx, struct agx_device *dev)
       dev->params.features = normalized_features;
    }
 
+   /* VM status is read with a direct GET_PARAMS ioctl on the device fd, which
+    * the virtio-gpu fd of a guest does not implement, so every check would
+    * report a lost device. */
+   if (dev->is_virtio)
+      dev->params.features &= ~(DRM_ASAHI_FEATURE_VM_STATUS |
+                                DRM_ASAHI_FEATURE_VM_STATUS_MIRROR);
+
    /*
     * Recognition, shader codegen, descriptors and the command stream are
     * independently versioned. A part is usable only once every required axis
